.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payouts-destinations-update - Change a destination's label, refund reserve or minimum


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payouts destinations update  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Change a payout destination's label, refund reserve or minimum deposit. Only the
destination's own wallet may.

.PP
--reserve and --min-amount are decimals in token units, converted with the
destination token's decimals. An empty value clears the field: --reserve ""
restores the gateway's suggestion, --min-amount "" removes the minimum.

.PP
CHANGING the minimum asks for the details confirmation again, exactly like 'add'
(a y/N prompt on a terminal, or --confirm-details; --yes does not count): the
minimum is copied from the venue, and a wrong one is how a deposit gets lost.
Re-sending the current value asks nothing. Raising it above the destination's
latest proof takes the verification away: the destination goes back to
"unverified" and needs a new proof at the new minimum.

.PP
To switch a destination off or on, use 'disable' / 'enable'.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm-details\fP[=false]
	Accept the details statement without a prompt (needed without a TTY or with --agent); --yes does NOT imply it

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for update

.PP
\fB-l\fP, \fB--label\fP=""
	New label

.PP
\fB--min-amount\fP=""
	New minimum deposit, decimal in token units ("" removes it); asks for the details confirmation

.PP
\fB--reserve\fP=""
	New refund reserve, decimal in token units ("" restores the gateway's suggestion)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payouts destinations update <destination_id> --label "Exchange (main)"
  rail0 payouts destinations update <destination_id> --reserve 50
  rail0 payouts destinations update <destination_id> --min-amount 25 --confirm-details
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payouts-destinations(1)\fP
